    "created_at": "2016-02-09T17:27:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-09T17:27:02Z",
    "body": "> Provided you still think it would be clearer to write out element's node document everywhere.\n\nYeah, I still think that would be nice.\n\n> perhaps I should look into if we can avoid returning two values, since that seems rather poor practice.\n\nYeah, just returning the record in most cases seems better, and then explicitly serializing by calling into the URL Standard when appropriate. But I'm not sure how much work that is compared to just going back to the old phrasing (with slightly updated terminology).\n",
