    "created_at": "2016-02-10T12:37:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-10T12:37:37Z",
    "body": "Not returning two values was too hard at this point. We should slowly move to use URL records everywhere and serialize them only when needed (e.g., the `<img>` section has several violations of this) and then make that change.\n\nI also think Worker and EventSource should be updated to use the URL parser directly. The way EventSource claims its second argument is optional is also bogus (since a dictionary will always be passed thanks to IDL). I plan to do some follow up for these once this is landed (easier to refactor then).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
